From f1620cf96c197f72429018cab981d4bc0a183c50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:20:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: raydium-rm692h5: Keep the panel's DSC RC range 0

The panel decodes DSC with its own config on page 0xd2. The driver as
picked rewrote RC range 0 to the VESA DSC 1.1 value {0, 4, 2} to match an
encoder that used it, but this tree's msm DSI host already programs the
DSC model's {0, 8, 2} at 10 bpc and 8 bpp (05ba9e9d212c), which is also
the panel's own value. The mismatch corrupted every detailed area of the
picture while flat areas decoded. Keep {0, 8, 2}.

(cherry picked from commit fefd0c304a1b111ea76e51083ead28a9844088e5)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-raydium-rm692h5.c | 11 +++++------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-raydium-rm692h5.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-raydium-rm692h5.c
index 9aa80e0e3d95..c97957fbe524 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-raydium-rm692h5.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-raydium-rm692h5.c
@@ -353,13 +353,12 @@ static void rm692h5_on(struct mipi_dsi_multi_context *dsi_ctx,
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0x72, 0x7e);
 	/*
 	 * Page 0xd2 holds the panel's DSC decoder config, which it appears to
-	 * use instead of the PPS we send.
-	 * RC range 0 is {min_qp 0, max_qp 8, offset 2} downstream, as in the
-	 * DSC model pre-SCR config; the kernel encoder uses the VESA DSC 1.1
-	 * value max_qp 4 (see drm_dsc_helper.c). Everything else matches, and
-	 * the mismatch corrupts the picture, so program {0, 4, 2} (0x0102).
+	 * use instead of the PPS we send. RC range 0 is {min_qp 0, max_qp 8,
+	 * offset 2} (0x0202), the DSC model's pre-SCR value that the msm DSI
+	 * host also programs at 10 bpc and 8 bpp; any other value corrupts
+	 * the picture.
 	 */
-	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0x73, 0x01);
+	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0x73, 0x02);
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0x74, 0x02);
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0x75, 0x22);
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(dsi_ctx, 0x76, 0x00);
-- 
